# SimLab: challenge answers

Every answer was run through the real simulation and passes its challenge. Anything not listed stays at its default. For a clean run, press **Reset**, set the values, then press **Play**.

---

## Cannon (50 XP)

### 1. Land a shot in the bucket at 40 m (15 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Launch speed | **19.81 m/s** |
| Angle | **45°** |
| Height / Gravity / Bucket | 0 m / Earth / 40 m |

*Why:* with no launch height, range = v² sin 2θ / g. At 45°, v = √(40 × 9.81) = 19.81 m/s.

### 2. On Earth, reach 100 m with a launch speed under 35 m/s (15 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Launch speed | **32 m/s** (anything from 31.4 up to 34.9) |
| Angle | **45°** |

*Why:* 45° gives the longest range. 32² / 9.81 = 104.4 m.

### 3. Hit the bucket on Mars with your first shot (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Gravity | **Mars, 3.71 m/s²** |
| Launch speed | **12.18 m/s** |
| Angle | **45°** |
| Bucket | 40 m |

*Why:* v = √(40 × 3.71) = 12.18 m/s. This shot also completes challenge 1.

> ⚠️ Only your first Mars shot counts. If you miss, move the bucket at least 5 m away from where your shots landed, then use v = √(distance × 3.71).

