## Springs and pendulums (55 XP)

### 1. Make the period 2.00 s, with no driving force (15 XP)
Use either option:

| Option | Settings |
|---|---|
| **Pendulum** | Length **0.994 m**, starting angle **5°** |
| **Spring** | Mass **1 kg**, spring constant **9.87 N/m** |

Damping and driving force stay at 0.

*Why:* T = 2π√(L/g), so L = g/π² = 0.994 m. Or T = 2π√(m/k), so k = π² = 9.87 N/m. Keep the swing small: a wide pendulum swing runs slow.

### 2. Resonance: swing more than 0.3 m with a drive of 1 N or less (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Mode | **Mass on a spring** |
| Mass / Spring constant | 0.5 kg / 20 N/m |
| Starting displacement | **0** |
| Damping | **0.2 kg/s** |
| Driving force | **1 N** |
| Driving frequency | **1.007 Hz** |

*Why:* the natural frequency is f₀ = (1/2π)√(k/m) = 1.007 Hz. The drive must be within 10% of it, and low damping lets the swing build up.

### 3. Critical damping: stop it fastest without overshoot (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Mode | **Mass on a spring** |
| Mass / Spring constant | 0.5 kg / 20 N/m |
| Starting displacement | **0.2 m** (at least 0.1) |
| Damping | **6.32 kg/s** |
| Driving force | 0 |

*Why:* critical damping is b = 2√(km) = 2√(20 × 0.5) = 6.32 kg/s. It's accepted within 5%.

