## Orbit sandbox (55 XP)

### 1. Circular orbit round a star of 3 suns or more (15 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Star mass | **4 suns** |
| Start distance | **1 AU** |
| Start speed | **59.57 km/s** |

*Why:* circular speed is v = √(GM/r), which is 29.78 × √(M/r) km/s. Let it go once round.

### 2. Period of exactly 2 years, within 1% (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Star mass | **1 sun** |
| Start distance | **1.587 AU** |
| Start speed | **23.64 km/s** |

*Why:* Kepler's third law gives T² = a³/M, so a = 2^(2/3) = 1.587 AU. Use circular speed there, 29.78 / √1.587 = 23.64 km/s.

### 3. Escape with the least extra speed (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Star mass | **1 sun** |
| Start distance | **3 AU** |
| Start speed | **24.6 km/s** (anything from 24.32 to 24.81) |
| Time scale | 5 yr/s (so you don't wait as long) |

*Why:* escape speed is √2 × circular speed = 42.12 / √3 = 24.32 km/s. You must reach it but stay within 2% above. The challenge completes once the planet has flown off.

