## Wave on a string (55 XP)

Wave speed with the defaults: v = √(T/μ) = √(4 / 0.1) = 6.32 m/s. The string is L = 2 m long.

### 1. 3rd harmonic with the right end free (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| What starts the wave | **Shake the left end** |
| Right end | **Free** |
| Driving frequency | **2.372 Hz** |

*Why:* with one end free, the harmonics are fₙ = n·v/4L for odd n. f₃ = 3 × 6.32 / 8 = 2.372 Hz. Wait for the pattern to settle.

### 2. A pulse comes back upright (15 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| What starts the wave | **Pluck a pulse** |
| Left end / Right end | **Fixed / Fixed** |

*Why:* each fixed end flips the pulse upside down. Two flips bring it back upright, about 0.63 s later.

### 3. Exactly 4 nodes between the ends (20 XP)
| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| What starts the wave | **Shake the left end** |
| Right end | **Fixed** |
| Driving frequency | **7.906 Hz** |

*Why:* with both ends fixed, fₙ = n·v/2L. The 5th harmonic has 4 nodes between the ends: f₅ = 5 × 6.32 / 4 = 7.906 Hz.

